From 518b2939c343d1952c20232c1625c35c8d75353f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:09:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: whnat: keep the vif slots across a PPE

mt76 registers a vif with en75_whnat_register_vif() once, when it adds
it, and ignores the error. That failed with -ENODEV while no PPE was
active, and airoha_whnat_clear_ppe() dropped every slot, so a vif added
before the PPE came up, or a PPE recreated by an unbind and bind of the
Ethernet device, left the WiFi traffic on the CPU until the vif was
added again.

Give the vif a slot whether or not a PPE is active: the frames already
fall back to the CPU while there is none. Keep the slots when the PPE
goes away, and drop the netdev references only when the module is
unloaded.

Found by a Codex audit agent. Checked with its user-space harness built
from these functions: a vif added before the PPE and a PPE recreated
keep slot 0 and hand frames once a PPE is active; a module unload drops
the reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b7f1ce7cb2cb65a65b2190bc5369fc3b87262bbd)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
index 13528a783..bd92d4d87 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
@@ -110,7 +110,15 @@ void airoha_whnat_clear_ppe(struct airoha_ppe *ppe)
 	RCU_INIT_POINTER(active_ppe, NULL);
 	synchronize_net();
 
-	/* The PPE flushes its flows itself; only drop the netdev references. */
+	/*
+	 * The PPE flushes its flows itself. mt76 registers a vif only when it
+	 * adds it, so keep the slots for a PPE that comes back (unbind and
+	 * bind); frames fall back to the CPU while there is none. Only drop the
+	 * netdev references when the module goes away.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_MODULE(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA) || module_is_live(THIS_MODULE))
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&vif_lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < AIROHA_WHNAT_VIFS; i++)
 		airoha_whnat_release_slot(i, false);
@@ -131,12 +139,16 @@ void airoha_whnat_clear_qdma(struct airoha_qdma *qdma)
 	synchronize_net();
 }
 
-/* Give a WiFi netdev a slot; the slot index tags its frames in the PPE. */
+/*
+ * Give a WiFi netdev a slot; the slot index tags its frames in the PPE. This
+ * does not need an active PPE: mt76 registers its vifs once, and a PPE that
+ * comes up later must still find them.
+ */
 int en75_whnat_register_vif(struct net_device *dev)
 {
 	int i, idx = -ENOSPC;
 
-	if (!dev || !rcu_access_pointer(active_ppe))
+	if (!dev)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	mutex_lock(&vif_lock);
